"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[25249],{325249:e=>{e.exports='# Job Run Diagnosis Skill\n\n## Use Available Context First\n\n`job_id` and `job_run_id` will almost always be in context. `errorMessage`, `stackTrace`, and `currentCodeBlock` are also provided when the user clicks "Diagnose error" — use all of these as your starting point. You do not need to fetch additional info if the context already contains enough to identify the root cause.\n\nIf the available context is insufficient to diagnose the issue and `<serverless_available>` is `true`, use the CLI to fetch more detail (preferred). If `<serverless_available>` is `false`, work with what is in context and use available tools as needed.\n\n## AI Diagnose\n\nWhen `<serverless_available>` is `true` and the `runAiDiagnose` tool is available, use it to debug Spark runtime related issues. This tool executes `AI_DIAGNOSE()` on serverless compute and returns root cause analysis with suggested fixes. Pass the run ID from context.\n\n## Fetching Run Details via CLI\n\nThe Databricks CLI is available via the `runDatabricksCli` tool, but only when `<serverless_available>` is `true`. When needed:\n\n- `jobs get-run {run_id} --output JSON` — Get run state and per-task status\n- `jobs get-run-output {run_id} --output JSON` — Get the full output and error details for a run; for multi-task jobs, use the task-level `run_id` from the `tasks` array in `get-run` output\n\nInspect the `state`, `tasks`, and use the task `run_id` to call `jobs get-run-output` for the specific failed task.\n\n## Before Responding\n\n1. If the error is unfamiliar or ambiguous, search for the error class or message in documentation.\n2. If the error references a table, view, or schema, verify it exists and the schema matches expectations.\n3. Trace the root cause as specifically as possible — reference the exact error, task, and line if available.\n\n## Response Format\n\n**Root Cause** — Always present. Be specific. Include an explanation of how you arrived at this conclusion — what context, tool outputs, or documentation informed the diagnosis.\n\n**Proposed Fix** — Only if the root cause is clearly established. Skip if multiple plausible causes exist and more info is needed.\n\n**Tip** — If `<serverless_available>` is `false`, briefly note that enabling serverless compute for this workspace would allow deeper diagnostics like fetching full run logs and task-level output.\n'}}]);
